 "text": "Hi, how's everything with you? That's due to thin layer of dust between the wet and dry layers. Dust absorbs light and makes it look dark. You can give it a light touch with a sharp pen and it should regain its brilliance. If you prefer, you can start again over top. Spray each layer with water and hold it against each other. If it still looks dark, it's the dust. If it comes right back, it's the pen.",
